{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1503413896,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUyNTE5ODcwMzE=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1748","origin":"github"},"title":"Simplistic demo of datalad crawler","message":"```shell\n# Google search for MRI .tgz brought to http://www.fmri-data-analysis.org/code\n# with boring list of urls to analysis code snippets and tarballs with data.\n# How to get that page useful content into a git/git-annex repository and be able\n# to update it if some erratum fixes get posted?\n\n# to get all text code snippets directly into git we use `--text-no-annex` switch\ndatalad create --text-no-annex handbook-fmri\ncd handbook-fmri\n\n# all urls of interest on that page seems to have `d=1` suffix, so we point crawler to  those\ndatalad crawl-init --save --template=simple_with_archives url=http://www.fmri-data-analysis.org/code 'a_href_match_=.*d=1$'\n\n# from now on crawler would know what to do\ndatalad crawl\n# you could now see code files from the page being added to git and \n# data files from tarballs to annex\nls\n# and upon rerunning the crawler, if nothing changed on the page, it should not do anything\ndatalad crawl\n```\n\n BTW, soon I would like to finish RF to meld `crawl-init` into `crawl --init`","files":null}]}